  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member who switches on the iCloud Keychain account sync, I want a switch-on that fails half-way to leave this device exactly as it was, so that another device's accounts never stay here while the switch reads off. Follow-up of LOT-173 (#312, PR #760), the Low points of the adversarial review's APPROVE (https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/760#issuecomment-6775004189).\n\n### Scope\n\n1. `AccountSync.merge` (switch-on over a full envelope): when the state save throws after the item write and the store merge, the rollback restores the item but not the device-only store. Restore the book captured before `accounts.update` in the same rollback; extend `aSwitchOnThatCannotSaveItsStateUnsharesTheAccounts` to check the store.\n2. The rollback over an absent item writes a tombstone dated at the new `enabledAt`, which switches off a device whose envelope was not delivered yet (fail closed): add one line to `docs/lots/LOT-173-keychain-sync-lock.md` (*Switch on*), or restore absence if the Keychain API allows deleting only this item safely.\n3. `AccountsModel.checkSessions`'s `loginSaves` fence has no app test: add one with the gated refresher (`CheckGate`) and an adopted sync report.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Each case has a test shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] Engine `swift test` and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n\n- Module: HFRStorage, App · post-MVP · depends on PR #760 merged.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
